1	# Hugging Face Hub Semantic Search MCP Server
2	
3	> **⚠️ Note**: This is an **unofficial** MCP server inspired by Hugging Face's official MCP server. It may be deprecated at any time if official functionality supersedes it. For the official server, see [hf.co/mcp](https://hf.co/mcp).
4	
5	An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides semantic search capabilities for Hugging Face models and datasets. This server enables Claude and other MCP-compatible clients to search, discover, and explore the Hugging Face ecosystem using natural language queries.
6	
7	## Features
8	
9	- **Semantic Search**: AI-powered similarity search (not just keyword matching)
10	- **Dataset Search**: Find datasets based on natural language descriptions
11	- **Model Search**: Find models with optional parameter count filtering
12	- **Similarity Search**: Find similar models/datasets to a given one
13	- **Trending Content**: Get currently trending models and datasets
14	- **Detailed Metadata**: Access comprehensive technical information via HuggingFace API
15	- **Model/Dataset Cards**: Download README cards for detailed information
16	
17	## Tools Available
18	
19	### Dataset Tools
20	- `search_datasets`: Search datasets using natural language queries
21	- `find_similar_datasets`: Find datasets similar to a specified one
22	- `get_trending_datasets`: Get currently trending datasets
23	- `get_dataset_info`: Get detailed metadata for a specific dataset
24	- `download_dataset_card`: Download README card for a dataset
25	
26	### Model Tools  
27	- `search_models`: Search models using natural language queries with parameter filtering
28	- `find_similar_models`: Find models similar to a specified one
29	- `get_trending_models`: Get currently trending models with parameter filtering
30	- `get_model_info`: Get detailed metadata for a specific model
31	- `get_model_safetensors_metadata`: Get model architecture details and parameter count from safetensors
32	- `download_model_card`: Download README card for a model
33	
34	## Installation
35	
36	### Prerequisites
37	- [UV](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) - Fast Python package installer
38	- Claude Desktop or another MCP-compatible client
39	
40	### Quick Start
41	No installation needed! UV will automatically fetch and run the server.
42	
43	## Configuration
44	
45	### Claude Desktop Setup
46	
47	Add the following to your Claude Desktop configuration file:
48	
49	**macOS**: `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`  
50	**Windows**: `%APPDATA%/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
51	
52	```json
53	{
54	  "mcpServers": {
55	    "huggingface-hub-search": {
56	      "command": "uvx",
57	      "args": [
58	        "git+https://github.com/davanstrien/hub-semantic-search-mcp.git"
59	      ],
60	      "env": {
61	        "HF_SEARCH_API_URL": "https://davanstrien-huggingface-datasets-search-v2.hf.space"
62	      }
63	    }
64	  }
65	}
66	```
67	
68	### Alternative: Local Development Setup
69	
70	If you want to contribute or modify the code:
71	
72	```bash
73	# Clone the repository
74	git clone https://github.com/davanstrien/hub-semantic-search-mcp.git
75	cd hub-semantic-search-mcp
76	
77	# Install dependencies with UV
78	uv sync
79	```
80	
81	Then configure Claude Desktop to use the local version:
82	```json
83	{
84	  "mcpServers": {
85	    "huggingface-hub-search": {
86	      "command": "uv",
87	      "args": [
88	        "--directory",
89	        "/path/to/hub-semantic-search-mcp",
90	        "run",
91	        "python",
92	        "app.py"
93	      ],
94	      "env": {
95	        "HF_SEARCH_API_URL": "https://davanstrien-huggingface-datasets-search-v2.hf.space"
96	      }
97	    }
98	  }
99	}
100	```
101	
102	## Usage Examples
103	
104	Once configured, you can use the tools in Claude Desktop:
105	
106	### Search for Datasets
107	> "Find datasets about climate change and weather patterns"
108	
109	### Search for Models
110	> "Find small language models under 1B parameters for text generation"
111	
112	### Find Similar Content
113	> "Find datasets similar to 'squad' for question answering"
114	
115	### Get Trending Content
116	> "Show me the top 10 trending AI models this week"
117	
118	### Get Detailed Metadata
119	> "Get detailed information about the 'stanford-nlp/imdb' dataset"
120	> "Show me technical details and configuration for 'microsoft/DialoGPT-medium'"
121	> "What's the parameter count and architecture of 'microsoft/DialoGPT-medium'?"
122	
123	### Download Documentation
124	> "Download the model card for 'microsoft/DialoGPT-medium'"
125	
126	## Environment Variables
127	
128	- `HF_SEARCH_API_URL`: Base URL for the search API (default: https://davanstrien-huggingface-datasets-search-v2.hf.space)
129	
130	## Search Backend
131	
132	This MCP server connects to a semantic search API that indexes Hugging Face models and datasets with AI-generated summaries. The search uses embedding-based similarity rather than keyword matching, making it more effective for discovering relevant content based on intent and meaning.
133	
134	## Development
135	
136	### Running Locally
137	```bash
138	# Run the server directly
139	uv run python app.py
140	
141	# Or activate the virtual environment
142	uv shell
143	python app.py
144	```
145	
146	### Testing with MCP Inspector
147	```bash
148	# Test the GitHub version
149	npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector uvx git+https://github.com/davanstrien/hub-semantic-search-mcp.git
150	
151	# Or test locally
152	npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector uv run python app.py
153	```
154	
155	## Contributing
156	
157	Contributions are welcome! Please feel free to submit issues and pull requests.
158	
159	### Development Setup
160	```bash
161	git clone https://github.com/davanstrien/hub-semantic-search-mcp.git
162	cd hub-semantic-search-mcp
163	uv sync --dev
164	```
165	
166	## License
167	
168	MIT License - see LICENSE file for details.
169	
170	## Related Projects
171	
172	- [Model Context Protocol](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk)
173	- [Hugging Face Hub](https://huggingface.co/docs/hub/)
174	- [Claude Desktop](https://claude.ai/download)
175	- [UV](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) - Fast Python package installer

